WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:08.200
Tiny cellulose crystals recovered from waste tissue are piezoelectric, making electricity when pressed, but on their own the effect is weak.

2
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:15.500
The team attached sulfate groups to the crystal surface, raising surface charge and aligning the dipoles.

3
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:24.700
The calculated dipole moment grew 3.4 times, and under the same force the voltage exceeded six times that of untreated crystals.

4
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:33.200
Mixed with carbon nanotubes and a polymer and coated on mulberry paper, the device produced 6 to 8 volts when pressed.

5
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:40.500
It read the wrist pulse, finger bending and neck movement, and kept its performance over twenty thousand cycles.

6
00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:47.500
One device harvests energy and senses motion, even sending a doorbell and safety line alert.
